# Frappe Framework & ERPNext Technical Rules

When generating, modifying, or reviewing code for Frappe Framework or ERPNext apps:

## 1. ORM & Database Access
- Use `frappe.get_doc(doctype, name)` to load a full document with children.
- Use `frappe.get_all(doctype, filters=..., fields=...)` for fast DB queries without permissions overhead, or `frappe.get_list` when permission filtering is required.
- Use `frappe.db.get_value(doctype, filters, fieldname)` for single field lookups.
- Use `frappe.db.set_value(doctype, name, fieldname, value)` for single-column updates without triggering full document events.
- Parameterized SQL only:
  ```python
  frappe.db.sql("""
      SELECT name, status
      FROM `tabTask`
      WHERE project = %(project)s AND status != %(status)s
  """, {"project": project_name, "status": "Closed"}, as_dict=True)
  ```

## 2. Controllers & Lifecycle
- Inherit controllers from `frappe.model.document.Document`.
- Standard lifecycle methods:
  - `before_insert(self)`: Before doc is inserted into DB.
  - `validate(self)`: Business logic validation before saving.
  - `on_update(self)`: After save (do NOT call `self.save()` here!).
  - `on_submit(self)`: Triggered when docstatus becomes 1 (Submitted).
  - `on_cancel(self)`: Triggered when docstatus becomes 2 (Cancelled).

## 3. Whitelisted APIs
- Decorate endpoints with `@frappe.whitelist(allow_guest=False)`.
- Always check permissions:
  ```python
  if not frappe.has_permission("Customer", "read"):
      frappe.throw(_("Not permitted"), frappe.PermissionError)
  ```

## 4. Client-Side Scripting (Desk JS)
- Always use the official form event framework:
  ```javascript
  frappe.ui.form.on('Task', {
      refresh(frm) {
          if (!frm.is_new()) {
              frm.add_custom_button(__('Mark Completed'), () => {
                  frm.set_value('status', 'Completed');
                  frm.save();
              });
          }
      },
      status(frm) {
          // Triggered on status field change
      }
  });
  ```

